The completed v1 checkpoint bundle and its 22 TRAIN development anchors are readable, as is the authenticated source corpus they bind. The key compatibility issue is now concrete: V0.25 exposes per-user legal masks and physical actions `(norad_id, beam_chain_id)`, but the sibling formula assumes a dense 7-beams-per-satellite action axis plus a separate `slot_cell`. I’m checking whether V0.25 actually records an equivalent topology, rather than silently substituting local shortlist indices.
