/home/sat/papers/modqn-paper-reproduction/docs/research/modqn-faithful-ablation/PILOT-LR-PROTOCOL-2026-08-15.md:28:- The pilot uses the z-enabled matched control: the 112-dimensional raw state is concatenated with its same-step cross-user per-feature z-score, yielding 224 dimensions. The raw-only 112-dimensional control is not part of the LR pilot.
/home/sat/papers/modqn-paper-reproduction/docs/research/modqn-faithful-ablation/PILOT-LR-PROTOCOL-2026-08-15.md:29:- Capacity penalty, Catfish EXP, and ACRM are all disabled. Therefore the pilot isolates the common MODQN substrate and learning rate.
/home/sat/papers/modqn-paper-reproduction/docs/research/modqn-faithful-ablation/PILOT-LR-PROTOCOL-2026-08-15.md:72:Any fence mismatch, stale artifact reuse, non-finite quantity, schema omission, or identity failure is `PROTOCOL-FAIL`; do not change the formula, runtime, golden data, thresholds, or hashes to force a pass.
/home/sat/papers/modqn-paper-reproduction/docs/research/modqn-faithful-ablation/PILOT-LR-PROTOCOL-2026-08-15.md:76:The pilot is not a search for the largest endpoint. Reject a learning rate if any seed shows numerical failure, persistent Q/target explosion, invalid physical metrics, or late-window collapse. Among remaining rates, prefer the smallest rate whose three-seed learning progress is consistently better by 3000 episodes and whose 100-episode ratio-of-sums trend has not already turned into a sustained decline. If the evidence is mixed, retain `0.001` as the conservative control and report that 3000 episodes did not identify a safe faster rate.
