     1	"""Fail-closed configuration for the MODQN-faithful Family-B ablation seam.
     2	
     3	This package is deliberately a sibling surface.  It does not modify the
     4	baseline ``TrainerConfig`` or any Family-B/runtime formula module.  The six
     5	arms below share the current Family-B protocol and differ only in the declared
     6	input/method treatment:
     7	
     8	``modqn_raw``
     9	    Auxiliary raw-base MODQN control.
    10	``modqn_z``
    11	    Matched MODQN control using the per-step cross-user z representation.
    12	``full``
    13	    Capacity penalty (P) + faithful item-replay experience machinery (EXP) +
    14	    linear matched-rollout ACRM.
    15	``wo_penalty``
    16	    EXP + ACRM, with P disabled.
    17	``wo_exp``
    18	    P only.  EXP and ACRM are both off; this is an explicit treatment, not a
    19	    silently downgraded catfish arm.
    20	``wo_acrm``
    21	    P + EXP, with ACRM disabled.
    22	
    23	The current physical EE/r1/r2/r3/calibration/RNG/contract values are inherited
    24	from the frozen Family-B preregistration.  ``load_ablation_config`` validates
    25	those values before a trainer can be built, so a stale or edited prereg fails
    26	closed instead of silently becoming a different experiment.
    27	"""
