/home/sat/.codex/sessions/2026/09/10/rollout-2026-09-10T18-04-05-01a08c7d-bb2c-74b0-bfda-4a795583216f.jsonl:9:{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:04:07.141Z","ordinal":8,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a08c7d-c265-7923-a7a8-92aa21382e03","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# PENALTY — assess the sibling project's top-k intent-tail regulariser as a C3 mechanism for this physics\n\nWorkspace `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-penalty-ws`. Interpreter\n`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python` only. **Never modify**\n`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover` or its `.venv`. **Design-phase assessment. Propose and price;\nimplement only a standalone probe, never a change to a sealed artefact.**\n\n**Resource limits.** **Hard cap: 3 python processes, `nice -n 16`, all BLAS threads = 1, peak\nRSS under 5 GB.** Six jobs are live. Print peak RSS and progress.\n\n## The candidate mechanism\n\nThe owner pointed at the sibling project's penalty design. Its source is\n`/home/u24/papers/modqn-paper-reproduction/src/modqn_paper_reproduction/modqn_faithful_ablation/capacity_penalty.py`\n— **if that path is not reachable from this machine, say so and work from the transcription\nbelow, marking every statement about it as transcribed rather than verified.**\n\nTranscribed shape:\n\n```\nvalues     = sum_i w_i * Q_i(x)                       # three heads, weighted\nnormalized = (values - mean) / (std + 1e-6)           # PER-USER z over VALID candidates only\nintent     = softmax(normalized / tau)                # soft differentiable intent per user\npressure   = index_add(intent -> (beam_rank, cell))   # aggregated ACROSS users\ntail       = row_sum - topk(pressure, k_cap, dim=cells)\nloss       = lam * sum((tail / users)^2)\n```\n\nIt is a **top-k physical-beam intent-tail regulariser**: it penalises intent mass falling\n**outside** the `k_cap` most-loaded cells, so it pushes **toward concentration**. Its docstring\nstates it \"never changes the environment's actual power/EE calculation\".\n\n## Why it is worth assessing here, stated as measured facts\n\n- **This physics rewards concentration.** `CROWDING-COST-2026-09-10.md`\n  (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-crowd-ws`): `d(EE)/d(active) = -425,009.885` bit/J per added active\n  beam over 8.00-98.25 beams, **no sign flip**; the most-crowded endpoint reaches\n  **46.110374 Mbit/J at full 1200/1200 service** versus 7.753232 at the spread endpoint.\n- **A jointly constructed profile beats the best per-user rule**: crowded endpoint 46.110374\n  versus `RSS_MAX` 41.621560, same panel, same full service — **+10.78%**.\n- **The current interaction route enters the decision as a single scalar** added to a sum over\n  ~100 per-user terms (`run_v025_pilot_c3.py`, ~1538-1568). This candidate is instead a\n  **structural cross-user coupling**.\n- **The current objective does not track EE**: `BASIN-BARRIER-2026-09-10.md`\n  (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-basin-ws`) found first-improvement started at `RSS_MAX` converges\n  **down** to 31.812902 from 41.621560, and the six-arm `F` order disagrees with the EE order.\n\n## Part 1 — read the real thing, do not trust the transcription\n\nVerify the transcribed math against the actual source, line by line. **Report any discrepancy**\n— the controller transcribed it after initially describing its direction backwards, and\ncorrected only on reading the tail computation. Treat that as a warning about this specific\nfile.\n\nReport: what `l_w`, `grid_count`, `k_cap`, `lam`, `tau` were set to in the sibling project, what\nits declared justification was, and **whether the sibling project ever reported it working** —\nthe config flags found were `\"capacity_penalty\": False` in several places, so establish whether\nit was an enabled treatment or a defined-but-off ablation arm. **If it was never enabled, say\nso plainly**: a mechanism that was designed but never demonstrated is a different proposition\nfrom one that was measured to work.\n\n## Part 2 — the mapping to this project, and its obstacles\n\nState precisely how each input would be obtained here:\n\n- the three heads → this project has Q1, Q2 and the interaction head. **Is the weighted-sum\n  form compatible with the sealed additive-plus-scalar composition, or would adopting it change\n  the composition?** That distinction decides whether this is a new route mechanism or a\n  redefinition of the existing one.\n- `action_mask`, `slot_cell`, `grid_count`, `beam_rank` → name the V0.25 fields, or say the\n  mapping is unavailable. **Do not invent one.** `MODQN-BRIDGE-2026-09-10.md` is the cautionary\n  case: it found 84 of 112 legacy fields unrecoverable and correctly refused to substitute.\n- the per-user z-normalisation is **internal to the penalty**, over valid candidates only.\n  Note that this is a third distinct use of z in this project, separate from the input-view\n  z-score, and that it carries **no capacity confound** because it adds no width.\n\n## Part 3 — a standalone probe, not an integration\n\nBuild a **read-only** probe that, on development anchors and existing frozen checkpoints\n(the completed v1 run at `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/artifacts/firstrun-500ep-20260910T1355Z`\n— **read it, never write into it**):\n\n1. computes the intent/pressure/tail quantities from the deployed heads as they are now;\n2. reports **the tail magnitude at the current policy** — if the tail is already near zero, the\n   penalty would never fire and the mechanism is inert here. **That is the first thing to\n   check and it may end the assessment.**\n3. reports the **correlation between tail and realised pooled EE** across anchors — does lower\n   tail actually mean higher EE on this panel, or is the relationship weak?\n\n**Do not train anything. Do not modify any arm, head, objective or sealed artefact.**\n\n## Part 4 — price it and name what it would change\n\nIf adopted, state: what it changes in the sealed inventory, whether it is a new route or a\nredefinition of C3, what has to be re-measured, and the wall-clock cost. **Do not recommend for\nor against** — the owner decides, and this exists so the decision is made with the price\nvisible.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Separate **verified by running code**, **transcribed**, **derived**, **inferred**.\n- **Compute no EE claim.** Loss values are never evidence about EE.\n- Development anchors only. **Do not read the 48 evaluation-only claim dates.**\n- **If the mechanism is inert here — tail already near zero, or the mapping unavailable — say so\n  first and plainly.** That closes a promising-looking line cheaply, which is worth more than a\n  hedged maybe.\n\nWrite to `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-penalty-ws/INTENT-TAIL-PENALTY-2026-09-10.md`, first line one\nbolded sentence stating whether the sibling ever enabled it, whether the input mapping exists\nhere, the tail magnitude at the current policy, and whether the mechanism could fire at all."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c7d-bbd3-7601-8dd6-a68d9aab7358","create_time":1789063447.1414511,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}}}
